{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/438596-frightened-condition-and-werewolves","id":438596,"title":"Frightened Condition and Werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-12T10:00:43-07:00","id":438596,"title":"Frightened Condition and Werewolves","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> This is extremely relevant to my current game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> How do people run the Frightened Condition if the Nosferatu were to target a Werewolf with Nightmare 2?<br /> <br /> Does it cause them to go full Gauru? Or is that only if they can't escape the source of their fear?<br /> <br /> 2e Werewolf preferably if you guys know that, but 1e will do in a pinch.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:27:07-07:00","id":438660,"title":"","content":"Does a scared werewolf go full Gauru? If the answer is yes, then we got our answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:31:11-07:00","id":438670,"title":"","content":"The werewolf would reflexively change to Urhan(or the form that allows for easier escape) and try to run away. If cornered I guess she will go berserk as the condition mentions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: If the power was used in combat maybe straight rage-mode would be more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 03-12-2015, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:40:58-07:00","id":438675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/438596-frightened-condition-and-werewolves?p=438670#post438670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The werewolf would reflexively change to Urhan(or the form that allows for easier escape) and try to run away. If cornered I guess she will go berserk as the condition mentions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: If the power was used in combat maybe straight rage-mode would be more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Imo, even in combat, it's still - best escape power. Only if escape is unavailable it goes to &quot;time to murderize those who stand in my path&quot; mode","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:48:00-07:00","id":438681,"title":"","content":"&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Supernatural creatures prone to loss of control, including<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">vampires, must roll to avoid frenzy. </span></span></span></span><br /> &quot;<br /> <br /> I believe that's what the question is about. It's made difficult since Kuruth no longer has a fear response equivalent.<br /> <br /> So, personally, I'd save that a werewolf enters Wasu-Im, in Urshul, and is immediately forced to make the Resolve + Composure rolls to attempt to do something else (in this case, running away), risking going into Basu-Im if they fail, unless it's not an option, in which case they'd attack normally.<br /> <br /> As a note, something from 1st edition, which may or may not still apply, is a rule that any supernatural power that makes a vampire enter frenzy makes a werewolf enter death rage, and visa versa. The differing rules now make it not as smooth a ruling, but I figured I'd note it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:17:07-07:00","id":438705,"title":"","content":"It's called Death <i>Rage</i> for a reason folks. Gauru comes in two flavours: Angry, and angrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:35:17-07:00","id":438726,"title":"","content":"There are two possibilities that I can see depending on whether or not the werewolf takes the &quot;other&quot; trigger and can recognize they are affected by Nightmare (a supernatural power) or not. In the first case, likely if the Nosferatu is the source of fear via Nightmare 1, then the werewolf would go death rage. In 2ed, it looks like they would turn into Urshul or Dalu for a brief period then Gauru behaving as falco was suggesting. This might be the default case in 1ed. In the second case, there is no reason for the werewolf to shift at all unless someone or something gets in it's way while fleeing. In any case, the werewolf isn't going to go Gauru because they were frightened, it is possible only because they got whammed by a vampire. A vampire frenzied over this power isn't going to behave differently than a mortal unless someone or something gets in their way either.<br /> <br /> You can really handle it any way you please. The werewolf can just run away, shift then run away fighting as needed to get away, or go &quot;Gauru smash&quot; all over the place. I would handle it differently depending on the situation. It could be fun to see a werewolf in death rage, but likely not.<br /> <br /> The key to note is the frightened condition does not cause death rage, using Nightmare can/does. Violence normally occurs only as a result of someone forcibly trying to keep the victim from running away. It is the <i>frightened</i> condition, not the angry condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T00:50:14-07:00","id":441067,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks guys, still doesn't seem to be a completely clear but we'll probably go for &quot;must use whatever resources are available to flee first, then Gauru if that's not possible&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:43:25-07:00","id":441899,"title":"","content":"Which part isn't clear? There is no definitive answer. Unless it is a player, it is best to just let the ST decide what is most appropriate. You have your options down. The werewolf either goes wolfman psychokiller or runs away and shifts as it is advantageous to get away safely. The inbetween forced shift is really only appropriate if the character is run by a player. I think you have it figured out well enough so go with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:01:32-07:00","id":441909,"title":"","content":"'Course, now some werewolves can have their rage triggered by getting <i>any </i>supernatural power used on them. Vamps call these guys &quot;land mines&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}